he Teammate holds a pair. Consequently, any pair I play will be unbeatable.\nIf I pass, and the Landlord holds {Black Joker, Ace}, he will clear the current trick, play the Ace, then the Black Joker to win immediately. To prevent this potential instant loss, I must take control of the game. By playing my pair of 10s, I can beat the 6s, and since no one else has pairs, I can continue to play my pair of Queens. This allows me to dictate the flow and set up a winning endgame (likely breaking my Aces to cover the Landlord\'s high cards).\n\nReason: Based on the unknown cards (BJ, A, 9, 7 all singles), the Landlord cannot have a pair. My pairs are invincible. Passing risks an immediate loss if the Landlord holds the high cards (BJ, A). Taking control guarantees I can deplete my hand significantly and counter the Landlord\'s remaining singles.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠10", "♥10"]}'}
